msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The names found by character identification are compared with each other. "
"Names that are similar enough are joined into one character group, such as I "
"Kancil and Kancil. The results show each group with the names it is called "
"by and how often it appears."
msgstr ""

msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The grouping is rule-based, so it needs no training data. A string "
"similarity method measures how alike two names are, and names whose "
"similarity reaches the threshold join the same group."
msgstr ""

#, python-format
msgid ""
"The default is %(method)s with a threshold of %(threshold)s, the best "
"setting for SatuaNER in the thesis (F1 %(f1)s, Tables 4.36 and 4.37). The "
"research mode offers all five methods and lets you change the threshold."
msgstr ""

msgid "Name similarity methods and their F1 scores in the thesis"
msgstr ""

msgid "Method"
msgstr ""

msgid "F1 with SatuaNER (Table 4.37)"
msgstr ""

msgid "Things to keep in mind"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Names with a suffix, such as Kakua and Kakuane, can end up in separate "
"groups, and general terms such as pekak can form a group of their own. Check "
"the groups before drawing conclusions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The model reads the satua word by word and marks the words that name a "
"character. Each name gets one of five entity labels:"
msgstr ""

#, python-format
